<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-12--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-glue-12: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57";
    dc:description "Head number under a defined bacterial treatment is a direct experimental endpoint, and the 2020 paper reports it for this commensal and for indole. Those measurements are not a deposited count table or expression series that can be reprocessed. The result can be reassessed from the publication and cannot be recomputed from open raw data.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Regenerate Dugesia japonica fragments exposed to the endogenous Aquitalea isolate or to indole, against microbiome-depleted controls, and score permanent two-headed anatomy. Two-headed animals specifically under the bacterium or indole, and not under depletion alone, would support hijacking of the default pattern; no change in head number would refute it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Indole has several host effects, so a two-headed outcome need not mean the morphogenetic circuit was overridden in the same way as a bioelectric rewrite.", "The RNA-seq mentioned with the indole treatment was not found as a public series, and head-number counts are in the paper.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.66"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.568"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-12--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2023-glue-12 by Grok 4.7: 0.5";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-12--grok>.
